WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.457
This query uses a regular expression to check the general shape of an email address.

00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:06.962
Rows that match are labeled valid shape.

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:09.092
Other rows are labeled review.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:11.612
The phrase valid shape is deliberate.

00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:19.332
A regex can check structure, but it cannot prove that the mailbox exists or that every possible valid internet

00:00:19.332 --> 00:00:23.627
email syntax is covered. Production validation rules should match the application requirements.

00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:27.557
String functions are most useful when the text has a predictable structure.

00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:32.337
Before extracting a substring, confirm the delimiter or pattern really exists.

00:00:32.337 --> 00:00:37.657
Regular expressions are powerful, but a complicated regex can become hard to maintain;

00:00:37.657 --> 00:00:41.440
use the simplest rule that reliably matches the data you actually have.
